# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real keys, then load it before running
# (e.g. `export $(grep -v '^#' .env | xargs)` on Linux/macOS), OR just export the
# variables directly in your shell. Both external APIs are OPTIONAL: the app runs
# and produces a full estimate without either, degrading gracefully.

# --- Metals.Dev (live copper/aluminum spot prices) ---
# Free tier, no credit card required. Sign up at https://metals.dev/ and copy the
# API key from your dashboard. Free tier covers copper, aluminum, lead, nickel, zinc.
# If unset, live copper pricing is skipped and copper cost is excluded from the total
# (clearly labeled in the UI), rather than the app crashing.
METALS_DEV_API_KEY=

# --- RentCast (OPTIONAL secondary parcel value lookup) ---
# Sign up at https://developers.rentcast.io/ and copy the API key.
# This is a secondary enhancement only. The regional-average land proxy always works
# without it. RentCast coverage for a raw, unaddressed coordinate is uncertain, so
# it is surfaced as a supplementary data point when available, not the headline value.
RENTCAST_API_KEY=

# --- Optional ---
# PORT=5000
